A||||19||skitime||Great day at the Mechanicsburg PA show||||1||
Z||000000||skitime||06-10-2001||09:51 PM||||We had a great time today.  We started the day meeting for breakfast with 11 Fieros and 15 people. It was a chance for many to meet fellow Pennocks members for the first time. We then had a cool 56 mile cruise to the show. We had a short rain shower to wash the road dirt off and then the wipe down to prep the cars.  We had 18 Fieros for the show a lot more than any other cars at the all Pontiac show. After the show we had a speedy cruise home.  Thanks to all those who got up early for the breakfast, we will try to set it up again.  Please post your pictures from this event we would love to see them.<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P6100024.jpg">    <BR>Early morning meeting for breakfast.<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P6100029.jpg">   <BR> Some of the sharp cars in the stock class.<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P6100033.jpg"> <BR>The modified Fieros.  Denny Lamberts Fiero in the foreground won first place.<P>The stock class winners were Jeff DeDay (Red 88 Fiero GT), Tom Derr (Red 88 Fiero GT), and Jen Gilbert (Black 85 Fiero GT),in that order.<P>The Modified class consisted of about 10 Fieros (give or take). Winners here were Denny Lambert (Silver 86 Fiero SE), Bob Schlag (Red 86 Fiero GT), and Jason Haughey (White 85 Fiero SE), in that order.  <P><BR>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg">    <P><p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 06-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Brucepts||06-10-2001||10:21 PM||||Skitime thanks for taking the time to organize the breakfast!!!! Enjoyed meeting everyone . . .  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Advanced Dealer in the Great Material Continuum . . .<BR>Non Fiero Website: <A HREF="http://tractorsport.com" TARGET=_blank>http://tractorsport.com</A> <BR>You can't race a dyno . . .||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierochic88||06-10-2001||10:49 PM||||Yes enjoyed meeting everyone from the Forum that I hadn't met previously and seeing those that I knew again!  Thanks for organizing breakfast guys!  Also, Vonnie - I think we need to raise our rates for judging  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Jennifer||||reg||1
Z||000003||Veronica's V6 GT||06-10-2001||11:11 PM||||I had a great time today and look forward to doing it again sometime. The cruise was so cool! Jennifer, I didn't realize that there's that much money to be made in judging. Now I can quit my full-time job and do this for a living.<P>Vonnie<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>88 GT<BR></UL><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Vonnies.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ditz88GT||06-11-2001||12:02 AM||||All I can say is WOW! What a great bunch of people with some very nice cars. I really had a good time and I hope to see everyone again soon.  I can't make Carlisle for all three days, in fact two may even be out of the question, but I do plan on going Saturday.  Maybe we could all meet up somewhere for breakfast again there?  Anyway, I just want to thank everyone for a wonderful time.  And as soon as I get my pics back and scanned I'll post them too.<P>Ditz88GT<BR> <A HREF="http://go.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://go.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000005||Denny||06-11-2001||10:43 AM||||Thanks for the great pictures, Dave!<P>And I'm beginning to think I paid too much for my trophy!  :^)<P>Seriously, I had a great time with all you nice Fiero folks.  Makes me feel guilty for not coming to breakfast.  Thanks for the fun!<P>And I apologize for the fast cruise home, but I don't get to drive the SE often, so I can't resist jumping on it a bit when I do.<P>See you all at Carlisle!<P>Denny||||reg||6
Z||000006||84Bill||06-11-2001||12:42 PM||||It was very nice to see everyone there at breakfast and the ride to Mechanicsburg was the best! I have some really cool pictures I'll put up on my web page along with the Videos I took. Just give me a day or so  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I managed to get a few pictures of what can only be described as a Fiero traffic jam on the ride home, both lanes packed with Fieros. I know you people were thinking I was nuts but I managed to get some great shots of us rolling down the highway. The Speed shot from the side of the road is really cool!<P>||||reg||14
Z||000007||skitime||06-11-2001||01:07 PM||||Hey 84Bill,  Anyway could I get a copy of the videos sometime.  Maybe from both of the shows.  I think thew would be awesome on a 32" TV.  Hmmm sounds like a Fiero road trip/cuise/picnic kind of idea to me. We could get together for a video viewing and curise the Amish country for more video oportunities.  Hmmmmm<p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 06-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||84Bill||06-11-2001||01:23 PM||||I'm going to try to get ALL my Fiero Videos on CD in MP3 or AVI format for distribution to who ever wants them. <BR>I heard a rumor of a Fiero curise / barbque non judged get together sometime in the future. Afterall we could never afford to pay Veroni and Jenn to judge it anyway.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000009||Brucepts||06-11-2001||02:13 PM||||Humm, cruisin' the Amish Countryside in our "Amish Ferrari"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>Here is an idea, we could all show up at one of the Zinns Park cruise nites maybe? I'll have to get a schedule of them.<P>------------------<BR>Advanced Dealer in the Great Material Continuum . . .<BR>Non Fiero Website: <A HREF="http://tractorsport.com" TARGET=_blank>http://tractorsport.com</A> <BR>You can't race a dyno . . .||||reg||1
